1
00:00:05,789 --> 00:00:09,393
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
"Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,195
Somehow... my body's gone numb...

3
00:00:12,362 --> 00:00:13,563
- Ran!
- Ran!

4
00:00:13,597 --> 00:00:15,032
Oi, are you okay?!

5
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:19,736
"If not given an antidote in time..."

6
00:00:19,803 --> 00:00:20,871
"...she will die."

7
00:00:21,038 --> 00:00:22,639
Ran!

8
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:26,309
Boy detective! Not yet?

9
00:00:26,576 --> 00:00:28,311
You don't know yet?!

10
00:00:30,047 --> 00:00:31,415
Cabaret club...

11
00:00:31,548 --> 00:00:33,083
What about a cabaret club?!

12
00:00:33,183 --> 00:00:35,218
There's only 40 seconds left.

13
00:00:35,485 --> 00:00:36,820
That's it!

14
00:00:36,987 --> 00:00:38,422
I've got it.

15
00:00:38,522 --> 00:00:39,890
This is...

16
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:48,565
Stop this already! What is this?!

17
00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:01,445
Anyhow, weren't you throwing
loving glances at Sensei to try and use him?

18
00:01:01,578 --> 00:01:02,512
Not really.

19
00:01:02,546 --> 00:01:05,449
Unlike a certain somebody,
I don't want to spread my body around.

20
00:01:06,783 --> 00:01:10,987
If you wanna deal in the sex trade,
I can grant your wish.

21
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:15,492
You're gonna be Number 2 for life, aren't ya?

22
00:01:18,895 --> 00:01:20,797
Crap woman! I'll kill ya!

23
00:01:20,897 --> 00:01:23,166
Kyoko! Stop it!

24
00:01:23,266 --> 00:01:24,134
Lemme go, I said!

25
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,470
I told all of you this, didn't I?

26
00:01:26,903 --> 00:01:31,308
I won't allow anyone to come between
me and Sensei.

27
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:35,445
He's...

28
00:01:36,146 --> 00:01:38,381
...my trophy.

29
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,555
Sensei.

30
00:01:45,622 --> 00:01:47,624
Huh? What is it?

31
00:01:47,724 --> 00:01:50,961
I have tomorrow off.

32
00:01:51,128 --> 00:01:52,963
Ah, I see...

33
00:01:53,296 --> 00:01:55,332
Do you have any plans?

34
00:01:57,267 --> 00:02:02,405
Should I...
come over to Sensei's home again?

35
00:02:02,772 --> 00:02:05,408
Ah... I wouldn't mind...

36
00:02:05,575 --> 00:02:07,077
Really?

37
00:02:07,177 --> 00:02:08,745
- Kanpai!
- Kanpai!

38
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,582
Damn...

39
00:02:12,749 --> 00:02:14,618
He's monopolizing Kumi-chan.

40
00:02:14,784 --> 00:02:16,419
Who on earth is that guy anyway?

41
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:20,390
When he first started coming in,
he was just a regular customer.

42
00:02:21,525 --> 00:02:23,827
Then he suddenly got rich...

43
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,295
That crap woman!

44
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:26,263
Eh?

45
00:02:26,296 --> 00:02:27,697
"Private Detective
Mori Kogoro"

46
00:02:27,797 --> 00:02:29,232
Did you just say something?

47
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:32,869
That story's already over.

48
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:33,937
"'Cristano' No. 2
Kyoko"

49
00:02:34,004 --> 00:02:37,307
More importantly, let's enjoy ourselves...

50
00:02:38,441 --> 00:02:39,776
How cute you are!

51
00:02:39,843 --> 00:02:41,878
I get that a lot.

52
00:02:41,978 --> 00:02:46,249
You're the worst, Dad...

53
00:02:46,783 --> 00:02:50,153
Look... Isn't it obvious your father's
a horrible cheater...

54
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:53,323
...so why are we sneaking in here
to investigate him?

55
00:02:53,623 --> 00:02:55,325
This is...

56
00:02:55,492 --> 00:02:59,496
This is only a major reconnaissance mission
that Mom asked us to do.

57
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:02,599
Fool! We're just here
to check up on his cheating.

58
00:03:02,632 --> 00:03:04,801
If you say that,
don't bring in the police anymore.

59
00:03:04,868 --> 00:03:06,469
"MPD Investigation Unit One - Takagi Wataru"
I'm sorry, Detective Takagi.

60
00:03:06,503 --> 00:03:09,639
Without you, we who are under 18
couldn't get into a store like this otherwise.

61
00:03:09,706 --> 00:03:11,441
So please don't get me involved in anything.

62
00:03:11,541 --> 00:03:15,245
If Sato-san saw me in a place like this...

63
00:03:15,545 --> 00:03:17,247
Excuse me...

64
00:03:17,881 --> 00:03:19,983
"'Cristano' Hostess - Kazuyo"
Thank you for waiting. I'm Kazuyo.

65
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:23,119
Ah, sit down, sit down...

66
00:03:23,186 --> 00:03:24,588
Excuse me.

67
00:03:26,556 --> 00:03:27,857
Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran

68
00:03:27,924 --> 00:03:31,061
Ah, by the way, that man there...

69
00:03:31,127 --> 00:03:33,330
He was a very popular
variety show host, wasn't he?

70
00:03:33,363 --> 00:03:34,297
"Official Mnemonic Challenge"

71
00:03:34,364 --> 00:03:35,832
"Beika University Science Department
Mathematics Department
Mine Masahito (Associate Professor)"

72
00:03:35,899 --> 00:03:36,967
Which reminds me...

73
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,402
Which reminds me, he also had a book published.

74
00:03:39,436 --> 00:03:42,539
Ehh... He seems to be very popular.

75
00:03:48,545 --> 00:03:50,447
Thanks for waiting!

76
00:03:50,547 --> 00:03:53,883
Now for the pride of this store, Game Time!

77
00:03:53,984 --> 00:03:57,721
Today's game is, Kiss-Kiss Derby!

78
00:03:57,854 --> 00:04:01,891
The lucky challengers are... these two!

79
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:06,363
Each challenger takes turns
receiving a kiss from...

80
00:04:06,463 --> 00:04:10,567
...each of the 20 girls lined up here
who then pour wine into their glasses.

81
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:15,071
Each challenger can choose between
1 to 3 girls per turn!

82
00:04:15,171 --> 00:04:16,940
Okay, let's do it!

83
00:04:17,007 --> 00:04:20,677
"'Cristano' No. 1 - Kumi"
For the one who reaches me, Kumi,
with their glass of wine...

84
00:04:20,810 --> 00:04:24,180
...will receive as their prize...
a kiss for a present.

85
00:04:24,247 --> 00:04:26,116
Wait for me, Kumi-chan!

86
00:04:26,182 --> 00:04:28,818
Because Kogoro-chan here'll be right there!

87
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:34,557
Um... How should we choose who goes
first and second? I don't mind either.

88
00:04:34,658 --> 00:04:36,559
You can go first.

89
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:38,361
Well then...

90
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:43,500
Then... just one.

91
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:46,336
The first challenger
cautiously picks just one girl!

92
00:04:46,503 --> 00:04:48,638
Just one? How chintzy...

93
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:51,107
Such a small person!

94
00:04:51,274 --> 00:04:55,945
I... will choose 3!
Shiori-chan, Karen-chan and Haruka-chan!

95
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:57,113
- Yes!
- Yes!

96
00:04:57,147 --> 00:04:58,915
He's suddenly chosen 3 girls!

97
00:04:58,982 --> 00:05:01,951
It's an explosion of sweet kisses!

98
00:05:03,186 --> 00:05:04,888
Then, I'll take two!

99
00:05:04,954 --> 00:05:09,059
A flower in both hands! A double kiss!

100
00:05:09,125 --> 00:05:11,161
Kogoro-san, hurry and come to me!

101
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:13,897
Of course you'll come to me, won't you?

102
00:05:13,963 --> 00:05:15,365
Of course!

103
00:05:15,432 --> 00:05:18,001
I'll take you on, one by one!
One after another!

104
00:05:18,134 --> 00:05:21,471
These three then:
Maria-chan, Saki-chan and Anna-chan!

105
00:05:21,538 --> 00:05:23,373
- Yes!
- Yes!

106
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:26,376
Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

107
00:05:30,647 --> 00:05:33,783
Somehow... I can't watch this anymore!

108
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:37,587
- Sir looks like he's having fun.
- I do envy him a little...

109
00:05:39,856 --> 00:05:42,592
Then...
I'll take one after another, too, with three girls!

110
00:05:45,228 --> 00:05:48,298
This has gotten good!
With this, that's 12!

111
00:05:48,331 --> 00:05:51,434
Kogoro-ojisama, hurry and take me away.

112
00:05:51,468 --> 00:05:52,469
Sure!

113
00:05:52,535 --> 00:05:54,704
As a man, I can take you all on!

114
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:58,541
Rina-chan, Misako-chan and Mao-chan, you three!

115
00:06:07,317 --> 00:06:10,420
They're slowly getting
closer to Kumi's lips!

116
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:11,988
15 down!

117
00:06:12,088 --> 00:06:13,556
Well then...

118
00:06:13,723 --> 00:06:14,691
Just one.

119
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:18,428
Ohh! Just one now!
That totals 16!

120
00:06:18,495 --> 00:06:22,065
The 16th one is Kyoko-san!

121
00:06:26,736 --> 00:06:28,805
She's inhaling his mouth!

122
00:06:45,588 --> 00:06:48,925
Yui-chan, Shoko-chan and Nagisa-chan...

123
00:06:49,225 --> 00:06:50,927
Huh? Ala?

124
00:06:51,428 --> 00:06:53,296
1, 2, 3...

125
00:06:53,363 --> 00:06:58,635
Too bad! There's no way you can
reach Kumi-chan now!

126
00:07:01,971 --> 00:07:05,575
I was certain Sensei would come to me.

127
00:07:11,915 --> 00:07:13,316
Damn!

128
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,772
Eh? Ah... Kumi-chan?!

129
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:37,774
- Kumi-chan!?
- Kumi-chan!?

130
00:07:38,141 --> 00:07:39,342
Everyone, please don't move!

131
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:41,344
Don't touch anything!
Detective Takagi, call the police.

132
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:42,312
Ah... yeah.

133
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:45,815
Boy detective?!
What are you doing coming here?

134
00:07:46,950 --> 00:07:48,151
She's dead...

135
00:07:48,184 --> 00:07:49,986
Kyaa!

136
00:07:57,961 --> 00:08:00,830
I'm sorry. I lost sight of myself...

137
00:08:01,097 --> 00:08:03,299
I guess she was poisoned?

138
00:08:03,366 --> 00:08:07,170
Most likely the poison was put into
the wine just before she drank it...

139
00:08:07,203 --> 00:08:08,705
What?! What! What! What?!

140
00:08:08,771 --> 00:08:10,974
Oi! that wine... I... I drank some of that, too!?

141
00:08:11,674 --> 00:08:13,843
A judge! No, a doctor! Where's a doctor?!

142
00:08:13,943 --> 00:08:14,777
Ah, I feel a sudden pain...

143
00:08:14,844 --> 00:08:16,212
Calm down!

144
00:08:16,312 --> 00:08:20,350
If there had been poison in your wine,
you'd be in the next world already.

145
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:22,218
Oh. Ah, that's right.

146
00:08:22,285 --> 00:08:26,022
Thanks to Kudo-kun, after the incident occurred,
not a single person has left this store.

147
00:08:26,122 --> 00:08:27,257
Yes.

148
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:29,926
The criminal should still be among us.

149
00:08:30,093 --> 00:08:31,628
Sato-san.

150
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:33,596
We've confirmed which decanter
contained the poison.

151
00:08:33,663 --> 00:08:34,497
Which one was it?

152
00:08:34,531 --> 00:08:36,366
Wait, boy detective!

153
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:39,969
This is an adult's society
where love and hate swirl.

154
00:08:40,136 --> 00:08:42,572
A kid like you should bow out.

155
00:08:43,006 --> 00:08:44,507
Kumi-chan's enemy...

156
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:50,446
This great detective, Kogoro Mori,
will surely pick them out!

157
00:08:52,282 --> 00:08:57,820
From your decanter,
a component of wolfsbane was detected.

158
00:08:57,921 --> 00:09:00,623
What's that?
I don't even know what that is.

159
00:09:00,690 --> 00:09:03,526
You had gotten into a dispute
with the victim today.

160
00:09:03,593 --> 00:09:04,827
So?

161
00:09:04,928 --> 00:09:08,631
Didn't you tell her?
That you would kill her or something...

162
00:09:09,265 --> 00:09:10,967
Hold on a minute!

163
00:09:11,067 --> 00:09:14,837
It's true I said that, but it'd be impossible
for me to seriously kill her, now wouldn't it?!

164
00:09:16,472 --> 00:09:20,843
A violent battle between women
unfolds on the battlefield for No. 1...

165
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:23,479
Doesn't that end in murder?

166
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:24,847
What's with that reasoning?

167
00:09:24,881 --> 00:09:28,785
Even if I became No. 1 that way, I'd just be
arrested and it'd be over, now wouldn't it?!

168
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,386
Thing is, if you're gonna say such things...

169
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:33,289
...then all of the cast and store assistants
would be suspects too!

170
00:09:33,856 --> 00:09:35,224
All of them?

171
00:09:35,258 --> 00:09:36,025
Yes.

172
00:09:36,125 --> 00:09:40,496
There isn't a single person in this store who
didn't resent or hate that crap woman.

173
00:09:40,964 --> 00:09:44,567
Then why was that poison in your decanter?

174
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:47,003
I don't know about that.

175
00:09:47,070 --> 00:09:52,508
I don't remember who it was that
gave me that decanter anymore...

176
00:09:52,609 --> 00:09:53,776
Liar!

177
00:09:53,810 --> 00:09:55,311
I'm not lying!

178
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:56,813
Excuse me.

179
00:09:57,046 --> 00:09:59,382
If I recall...

180
00:10:00,216 --> 00:10:01,985
...Kyoko-san, you were in this position, right?

181
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:04,687
Oi, boy detective!
What on earth is this about?!

182
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:07,690
It's important.
Please remember carefully.

183
00:10:08,057 --> 00:10:11,027
Down from that woman was...

184
00:10:11,761 --> 00:10:14,998
Nagisa, Shoko, and Yui.

185
00:10:15,098 --> 00:10:18,935
And, I think I was probably here.

186
00:10:19,102 --> 00:10:22,705
How did you end up as number 16?
How did you decide that?

187
00:10:22,839 --> 00:10:26,209
No reason really.
I was always just right around that point.

188
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:29,479
I see...

189
00:10:29,612 --> 00:10:30,813
Kudo-kun.

190
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,683
What meaning is there to position 16?

191
00:10:33,983 --> 00:10:38,354
In this game,
the one who gets to 16 is the winner.

192
00:10:38,988 --> 00:10:42,759
Once you get to 16, there's only 4 people left.

193
00:10:42,859 --> 00:10:46,629
Since between 1 to 3 people
can be chosen in each turn...

194
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:48,631
...that leaves between 1 and 3.

195
00:10:48,698 --> 00:10:51,067
You absolutely couldn't reach 20!

196
00:10:51,134 --> 00:10:52,735
That's how it is.

197
00:10:52,835 --> 00:10:56,339
In other words, by putting the poison
into number 16's decanter...

198
00:10:56,506 --> 00:10:59,809
...you would surely kill Kumi-san.

199
00:11:00,009 --> 00:11:03,479
The criminal is a logical thinker...

200
00:11:03,613 --> 00:11:06,716
...and at the very least
is someone good in mathematics.

201
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:10,687
Good in mathematics...

202
00:11:12,789 --> 00:11:14,624
The criminal...

203
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:16,826
...is you!

204
00:11:16,893 --> 00:11:19,629
I'm the criminal because I'm good at math?

205
00:11:19,862 --> 00:11:21,831
That isn't logical at all!

206
00:11:21,898 --> 00:11:25,435
Thing is, I was in love with her,
so I couldn't kill her, now could I?

207
00:11:25,535 --> 00:11:28,137
If you were in love with her...

208
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:31,207
...did she necessarily feel the same for you?

209
00:11:31,374 --> 00:11:34,510
To Kumi-chan, maybe you were just
a good customer who punctually paid his bills...

210
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,512
That is definitely not true!

211
00:11:38,648 --> 00:11:41,517
"Only reason makes us human."

212
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,788
Please excuse me for what I've done.

213
00:11:45,855 --> 00:11:48,758
"Doubt is the beginning of knowledge."

214
00:11:49,192 --> 00:11:51,527
There's also that quote, isn't there?

215
00:11:51,828 --> 00:11:53,296
You are...

216
00:11:54,764 --> 00:11:58,000
And? What did you want to ask?

217
00:11:58,267 --> 00:12:01,838
Mine-san, do you know
the underlying rule of that game?

218
00:12:01,938 --> 00:12:03,172
Yes.

219
00:12:03,406 --> 00:12:07,176
When you put it in
numerical formula form, it's n=4-r.

220
00:12:07,276 --> 00:12:11,247
n is the number that you take,
and r is the number the other person takes.

221
00:12:11,547 --> 00:12:15,852
But, if a person who knows
the game's rules plays second...

222
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,054
...then you couldn't win against them.

223
00:12:18,788 --> 00:12:20,556
Let's see... In other words...

224
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:23,159
One person in each round
can pick between 1 and 3.

225
00:12:23,226 --> 00:12:25,661
Therefore, if you're in the second spot...

226
00:12:25,728 --> 00:12:27,230
...you can pick a number that gives you
a multiple of 4 so that 4 is chosen each round...

227
00:12:27,263 --> 00:12:29,132
Even if you say that, I don't understand it!

228
00:12:29,198 --> 00:12:31,267
At any rate, if you went first,
you could win, right?

229
00:12:31,334 --> 00:12:32,401
That's how it is...

230
00:12:32,435 --> 00:12:36,239
Anyhow, even if you weren't a mathematician
and just gave it a little thought...

231
00:12:36,305 --> 00:12:39,175
...it seems anyone could come up with
the winning strategy.

232
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,678
That doesn't make me the criminal.

233
00:12:42,745 --> 00:12:44,847
You were at this store the entire time,
weren't you? Didn't you notice anything?

234
00:12:44,881 --> 00:12:45,948
I wasn't here...

235
00:12:45,982 --> 00:12:47,116
Damn...

236
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:49,652
Either Kyoko or Mine should be the criminal...

237
00:12:49,719 --> 00:12:52,955
Hey! Um... It would be a problem if
you used your cell phone.

238
00:12:53,055 --> 00:12:55,792
It's just a business e-mail,
so don't be a bother.

239
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:59,262
Something's... weird...

240
00:12:59,428 --> 00:13:00,863
What is it?

241
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,432
Even though one of their friends was killed...

242
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:06,235
...none of them seems to feel sad about it...

243
00:13:12,608 --> 00:13:14,610
Hey, Mao-chan, what are you doing?!

244
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:16,579
She's dead, so it's okay now, isn't it?

245
00:13:16,646 --> 00:13:18,681
I don't wanna see her face even a second longer.

246
00:13:18,748 --> 00:13:20,850
Wai... that's important evidence.
Weren't you told not to touch things?

247
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:24,387
Why would men want to come
to a place like this?

248
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,222
Why is that!?

249
00:13:26,622 --> 00:13:29,826
Hey, Dad, why is it?

250
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:32,195
Oi, oi! Don't be irresponsible!

251
00:13:32,295 --> 00:13:34,230
Let me go!

252
00:13:34,297 --> 00:13:36,232
Now, now, stop it...

253
00:13:42,638 --> 00:13:45,107
That hurt, you stupid woman...

254
00:13:47,710 --> 00:13:48,711
Huh?

255
00:13:55,218 --> 00:13:58,421
I can smell it...

256
00:13:58,521 --> 00:14:00,423
The scent of scandal...

257
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:08,264
What are you doing there so sneakily!

258
00:14:12,568 --> 00:14:14,370
What did you hide just now?!

259
00:14:14,537 --> 00:14:18,708
Don't think the eyes of this great detective,
Kogoro Mori, can be deceived!

260
00:14:18,841 --> 00:14:20,610
You're wrong.
This has nothing to do with that!

261
00:14:20,676 --> 00:14:21,844
Liar!

262
00:14:21,878 --> 00:14:24,146
This is evidence that shouldn't be moved...

263
00:14:24,647 --> 00:14:25,882
Ala?

264
00:14:26,649 --> 00:14:27,884
A cat?

265
00:14:28,384 --> 00:14:31,387
There seemed to be something wrong
with him, so I came to check on him.

266
00:14:31,888 --> 00:14:34,724
Please! Don't tell anyone.

267
00:14:41,664 --> 00:14:45,401
That high school student boy...
You called him Kudo-kun, right?

268
00:14:45,468 --> 00:14:49,171
Eh? Ah, yes. Kudo Shin'ichi.

269
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,173
Could it be...

270
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:53,175
...that you love him?

271
00:14:53,876 --> 00:14:55,144
Huh?!

272
00:14:55,177 --> 00:14:56,879
What is this out of the blue?

273
00:14:56,913 --> 00:15:00,650
It's nothing like love really.
He's such a detective geek.

274
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:03,252
Really? In that case, it's fine, but...

275
00:15:03,753 --> 00:15:07,290
"Irresolution causes
the greatest harm," they say.

276
00:15:07,757 --> 00:15:10,526
Eh... "Irresolution"?

277
00:15:10,927 --> 00:15:13,696
When you're indecisive
and can't make up your mind.

278
00:15:13,963 --> 00:15:15,598
Ah...

279
00:15:15,698 --> 00:15:18,267
That's irresolution, huh?

280
00:15:18,801 --> 00:15:21,037
When it comes to love...

281
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:24,106
I wonder if it's when you don't say
what should be said...

282
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:28,978
...and when you don't do
what you should do and then regret it?

283
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:34,583
Sir, you're a detective, aren't you?

284
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:38,554
A great detective.
It's a problem if you forget my name.

285
00:15:38,821 --> 00:15:42,191
Um... I... might know who the criminal is.

286
00:15:42,325 --> 00:15:43,659
Huh?!

287
00:15:47,797 --> 00:15:49,665
What's that?!

288
00:15:50,466 --> 00:15:54,236
This great detective, Kogoro Mori,
will now tell you!

289
00:15:54,437 --> 00:15:57,673
The one and only truth!

290
00:15:58,107 --> 00:15:59,442
Like I thought...

291
00:15:59,575 --> 00:16:01,844
The criminal is you!

292
00:16:02,611 --> 00:16:06,449
Sir...
Of course you can tell us your reason?

293
00:16:06,515 --> 00:16:09,085
It's as obvious as Maeda Atsuko-chan!
(member of AKB48 and an actress)

294
00:16:09,185 --> 00:16:10,886
She is in their top rank.

295
00:16:11,153 --> 00:16:12,955
So green and immature...

296
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:15,358
You wouldn't know this...

297
00:16:15,491 --> 00:16:20,096
...but this man caused a similar incident
using the same trick one month ago!

298
00:16:21,464 --> 00:16:23,566
"Then... I'll go second!"

299
00:16:23,699 --> 00:16:25,501
"Kazuyo, you go ahead."

300
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:27,636
"Then..."

301
00:16:28,371 --> 00:16:30,539
"...I'll take two."

302
00:16:34,677 --> 00:16:35,845
"Two!"

303
00:16:35,945 --> 00:16:36,779
"One."

304
00:16:36,846 --> 00:16:37,813
"Three!"

305
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,715
"Then I'll take 3 as well!"

306
00:16:39,782 --> 00:16:40,616
"One."

307
00:16:40,683 --> 00:16:41,584
"Two."

308
00:16:41,650 --> 00:16:43,586
"I'll take two, too."

309
00:16:45,187 --> 00:16:47,590
"I lost, didn't I?"

310
00:16:47,723 --> 00:16:49,492
"Too bad!"

311
00:16:49,892 --> 00:16:52,261
"Here. Your penalty game."

312
00:16:56,032 --> 00:16:57,967
"You don't have to drink it."

313
00:17:10,246 --> 00:17:12,248
"Kazuyo, are you okay?!"

314
00:17:12,314 --> 00:17:14,483
"Kazuyo?! Are you okay?!"

315
00:17:14,550 --> 00:17:18,320
Fortunately it wasn't anything that put
Kazuyo-san's life in danger.

316
00:17:18,521 --> 00:17:22,691
Kazuyo-san was famous for trying to get
nominated for the No. 1 spot...

317
00:17:22,825 --> 00:17:27,897
...but this guy from some time before had
wanted the nomination switched to Kumi-chan.

318
00:17:28,030 --> 00:17:31,367
And so you tried to kill Kazuyo-san
for interfering with that.

319
00:17:31,434 --> 00:17:32,768
That's right, isn't it?

320
00:17:32,902 --> 00:17:34,904
Ah, truly nasty.

321
00:17:35,004 --> 00:17:38,040
And then it appeared that
Kumi-chan had gotten it.

322
00:17:38,107 --> 00:17:43,612
However, turned out this guy's money
was all Kumi-chan was interested in.

323
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:47,650
Now this time he got angry at
Kumi-chan and killed her!

324
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,151
That's right, isn't it?

325
00:17:49,251 --> 00:17:52,922
The cocktail Kazuyo-chan drank...

326
00:17:53,089 --> 00:17:54,323
...was a Salty Dog.

327
00:17:54,423 --> 00:17:55,991
What about it?

328
00:17:56,425 --> 00:17:59,361
She has high blood pressure and she normally
has to take anti-hypertension drugs...

329
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:02,431
In other words, she was taking pills
to lower her blood pressure.

330
00:18:02,565 --> 00:18:05,568
Could it be...
Kazuyo-san had an interaction?

331
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:07,503
As expected. That's correct.

332
00:18:07,603 --> 00:18:09,738
Don't... Don't ignore me.

333
00:18:10,072 --> 00:18:11,607
What's the recipe for a Salty Dog?

334
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:12,775
Vodka and...

335
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:14,777
- Grapefruit juice!
- Right!

336
00:18:14,844 --> 00:18:16,545
Grapefruit juice...

337
00:18:16,645 --> 00:18:18,981
...when drunk in conjunction with certain types
of drugs, can strengthen their effectiveness...

338
00:18:19,081 --> 00:18:20,349
...and make them dangerous.

339
00:18:20,416 --> 00:18:21,584
Dangerous?

340
00:18:21,617 --> 00:18:25,187
Could it be Kazuyo-san's...
blood pressure fell too much and...

341
00:18:25,221 --> 00:18:27,056
She lost consciousness.

342
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:36,132
"Who on earth is it?"

343
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,668
"And for what reason?"

344
00:18:41,670 --> 00:18:44,473
Have you had
high blood pressure for some time?

345
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,741
Yes.

346
00:18:45,808 --> 00:18:49,445
So... I can't fail to take these each day.

347
00:18:49,612 --> 00:18:54,683
We've heard that recently you played
a game with Mine-san and then collapsed...

348
00:18:57,086 --> 00:19:01,891
"Irresolution causes the greatest harm," huh...

349
00:19:02,858 --> 00:19:04,126
What did you say just now?!

350
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:06,629
Eh? Ah... Irresolution.

351
00:19:06,695 --> 00:19:08,831
When you can't make up your mind...

352
00:19:09,031 --> 00:19:12,468
"Irresolution causes the greatest harm..."

353
00:19:13,435 --> 00:19:14,937
Who told you that quote?

354
00:19:15,004 --> 00:19:18,807
Huh? Ah... I learned it earlier
from Kazuyo-san...

355
00:19:18,874 --> 00:19:21,310
...but I didn't know what
the word "irresolution" meant...

356
00:19:25,014 --> 00:19:26,849
I see...

357
00:19:28,050 --> 00:19:30,819
The answer to this murder equation...

358
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:34,557
I know what the one and only truth is.

359
00:19:40,196 --> 00:19:42,198
Sorry for keeping you waiting.

360
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:45,734
Kudo-kun...

361
00:19:46,135 --> 00:19:48,904
Are you suspicious of me, too?

362
00:19:49,505 --> 00:19:52,441
There's one thing I really wanted to ask you.

363
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:54,643
Go ahead.

364
00:19:55,144 --> 00:20:00,449
That game one month ago
where Kazuyo-san collapsed.

365
00:20:00,516 --> 00:20:02,952
Did you know it was Kazuyo-san
who suggested she play that game?

366
00:20:03,652 --> 00:20:04,653
Eh?!

367
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,255
"Kanpai."

368
00:20:08,190 --> 00:20:11,393
"Since Mine-sensei loves that game so much,
I'm sure to rise."

369
00:20:11,493 --> 00:20:14,029
"Yes. Then, do you want to challenge Kumi?"

370
00:20:14,096 --> 00:20:15,231
"Yeah."

371
00:20:15,564 --> 00:20:19,068
The one who chose the penalty game
of a cocktail was also Kazuyo-san.

372
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:19,969
"Kumi"

373
00:20:20,536 --> 00:20:23,405
"Then, a Salty Dog, please."

374
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:26,675
Why would she do such a dangerous thing?

375
00:20:27,676 --> 00:20:31,847
Didn't Kazuyo-san want to
play that game as a test?

376
00:20:32,047 --> 00:20:34,183
A test? Of what?

377
00:20:35,684 --> 00:20:37,620
Your feelings.

378
00:20:39,688 --> 00:20:42,891
Kazuyo-san was aware of the dangers in the test.

379
00:20:42,992 --> 00:20:45,594
What would be Mine-san's choice?

380
00:20:45,728 --> 00:20:46,662
Would it be Kumi-san?

381
00:20:46,695 --> 00:20:51,233
"If you let me win,
I'll go out with you anywhere afterwards."

382
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:56,505
You immediately understood
the underlying rule of that game.

383
00:20:56,605 --> 00:21:00,776
So you could somehow
turn the win over to her.

384
00:21:05,281 --> 00:21:09,718
Since you knew about
the drugs she was taking...

385
00:21:09,785 --> 00:21:12,488
...Kazuyo-san believed you wouldn't
deliberately allow her to lose.

386
00:21:13,088 --> 00:21:15,958
However, the one Mine-san chose...

387
00:21:16,058 --> 00:21:17,960
...was Kumi-san.

388
00:21:21,897 --> 00:21:24,099
The criminal who killed Kumi-san...

389
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:27,036
You already know who that is, don't you?

390
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:31,507
The criminal is... you.

391
00:21:31,907 --> 00:21:35,611
The criminal is... you.

392
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:43,185
Kazuyo...

393
00:21:44,153 --> 00:21:45,487
Mine-san said it.

394
00:21:45,587 --> 00:21:48,357
That the hypertension drugs
you were taking were tablets.

395
00:21:48,490 --> 00:21:52,127
But the ones you have today
are capsules, aren't they?

396
00:21:52,594 --> 00:21:56,165
The poison is inside those capsules, isn't it?

397
00:21:56,865 --> 00:21:59,401
- Takagi-kun, confirm that.
- Roger.

398
00:22:01,337 --> 00:22:05,641
It was Descartes that made me realize
the relationship between you and Mine-san.

399
00:22:06,241 --> 00:22:08,844
Descartes? What's that?

400
00:22:09,211 --> 00:22:10,913
Rene Descartes.

401
00:22:11,213 --> 00:22:14,283
A great mathematician that I admire.

402
00:22:14,516 --> 00:22:19,521
"Only reason makes us human."
"Doubt is the beginning of knowledge."

403
00:22:19,655 --> 00:22:22,458
Those are both quotes from Descartes.

404
00:22:22,558 --> 00:22:25,961
And...
So is the quote Kazuyo-san told Ran.

405
00:22:26,028 --> 00:22:28,664
"Irresolution is the cause of the greatest harm."

406
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:31,867
Yes. That's also a quote from Descartes.

407
00:22:32,234 --> 00:22:35,003
Kazuyo-san, didn't you eagerly
study mathematics...

408
00:22:35,037 --> 00:22:38,841
... in order to follow along with
Mine-san's conversations?

409
00:22:39,375 --> 00:22:41,243
"Merry Christmas!"

410
00:22:41,343 --> 00:22:43,245
"Ah, Kazuyo-chan..."

411
00:22:48,684 --> 00:22:49,885
"What is that?"

412
00:22:49,952 --> 00:22:52,087
"Ah, it's nothing..."

413
00:22:52,254 --> 00:22:56,325
"You could say...
it's a direct coordinate system..."

414
00:22:56,392 --> 00:22:59,128
"You could also call them
Cartesian coordinates..."

415
00:22:59,228 --> 00:23:03,365
"They were created by Descartes,
but they're also called Cartesian coordinates..."

416
00:23:03,499 --> 00:23:06,935
"Because I'm stupid,
I didn't do well in math..."

417
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:09,505
"Ah... That's okay!"

418
00:23:09,705 --> 00:23:14,176
"Compared to human relationships,
mathematics is easy to understand."

419
00:23:15,277 --> 00:23:17,079
"Please teach me more."

420
00:23:17,212 --> 00:23:19,615
Ever since I had started at this job...

421
00:23:20,082 --> 00:23:25,387
...there wasn't anyone who had
talked to me so seriously like he did.

422
00:23:27,689 --> 00:23:29,491
I just...

423
00:23:29,725 --> 00:23:31,493
...wanted to keep up with him.

424
00:23:32,795 --> 00:23:34,663
Kazuyo...

425
00:23:35,697 --> 00:23:38,901
And so she thought up this crime.

426
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:44,773
Kazuyo-san. To you, it didn't matter who it was
that ended up as number 16, did it?

427
00:23:46,875 --> 00:23:49,845
What's more, you could say you didn't care...

428
00:23:49,945 --> 00:23:52,815
...if it was Mine-san or Ran's father
who gave the wine to Kumi-san.

429
00:23:53,916 --> 00:23:59,488
Whoever had the 16th spot with the poison in it,
Kumi-san, in the 20th spot, was sure to drink it.

430
00:23:59,655 --> 00:24:03,292
That was all that was
important to you, Kazuyo-san.

431
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,962
Killing Kumi-chan...

432
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:10,699
Was that your goal in doing that?

433
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,870
Resentment for the one who took
the man you loved away...

434
00:24:15,270 --> 00:24:17,806
That was your motive, right?

435
00:24:19,241 --> 00:24:23,145
There was nothing I could do if he chose
a woman more beautiful than I.

436
00:24:23,312 --> 00:24:26,148
I'm used to that happening...

437
00:24:26,548 --> 00:24:28,617
Then why Kumi-chan?

438
00:24:29,418 --> 00:24:32,120
By chance, I overheard her.

439
00:24:32,254 --> 00:24:35,958
"That Sensei's loaded..."

440
00:24:36,458 --> 00:24:39,695
"...so whether to Italy or Paris,
anywhere we wanna go'll be fine, Kenji."

441
00:24:39,828 --> 00:24:43,298
"I think I'll have him cough up
all the funds for a nice apartment, too."

442
00:24:43,365 --> 00:24:45,300
Such a dirty trick to play on Mine-san...

443
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:47,970
I never wanted him to hear that.

444
00:24:48,470 --> 00:24:52,407
I thought, "I never want him to have to
go through such a bad time."

445
00:24:57,145 --> 00:24:59,615
In order to protect Mine-san...

446
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:02,217
You killed Kumi-san?

447
00:25:03,952 --> 00:25:07,923
Like the game one month ago
where Mine-san made his decision...

448
00:25:08,957 --> 00:25:11,159
I decided, too.

449
00:25:11,860 --> 00:25:13,629
Why...?

450
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:17,399
Why would you kill someone for my sake...

451
00:25:17,966 --> 00:25:20,435
I'm the bad one...

452
00:25:23,105 --> 00:25:26,875
"Only reason makes us human."

453
00:25:28,410 --> 00:25:31,813
I'm sorry you went to
all the trouble to teach me that.

454
00:25:35,651 --> 00:25:39,054
I guess it's because I am stupid after all...

455
00:26:08,717 --> 00:26:10,452
Kazuyo...

456
00:26:11,887 --> 00:26:13,555
I'm sorry...

457
00:26:22,397 --> 00:26:24,232
"Kumi"

458
00:26:24,433 --> 00:26:26,535
"Kazuyo"

459
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:32,074
Sir.

460
00:26:32,307 --> 00:26:36,011
Why do you think Kazuyo-san would do that?

461
00:26:36,378 --> 00:26:41,049
Rather than murder,
wouldn't there have been a much easier way...

462
00:26:41,350 --> 00:26:44,219
You said it earlier, didn't you?

463
00:26:45,387 --> 00:26:47,589
For the sake of the man she loved...

464
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:50,392
...she studied mathematics
with all her might, didn't she?

465
00:26:51,226 --> 00:26:54,529
She wanted to be of use to him
at the end, no matter what...

466
00:26:54,796 --> 00:26:56,531
That's how it was.

467
00:26:56,965 --> 00:26:59,001
Why?

468
00:26:59,635 --> 00:27:04,473
By doing that,
he'd remember her all his life...

469
00:27:06,208 --> 00:27:09,911
Even if you're called a great detective,
I guess you are still a kid, huh?

470
00:27:10,245 --> 00:27:13,015
Don't think that everything comes
with a clear explanation.

471
00:27:13,448 --> 00:27:16,084
Humans aren't mathematics.

472
00:27:16,385 --> 00:27:21,423
Do you know what the most troublesome thing
in people that can't be calculated is?

473
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:25,227
What's that?

474
00:27:26,094 --> 00:27:28,597
A woman's heart.

475
00:27:28,964 --> 00:27:30,866
Huh?

476
00:27:33,669 --> 00:27:35,470
What about you, Shin'ichi?

477
00:27:37,205 --> 00:27:42,044
In order to protect someone
you loved, would you kill?

478
00:27:44,212 --> 00:27:46,281
No matter what the reason is...

479
00:27:47,182 --> 00:27:49,351
...murder is murder.

480
00:27:53,455 --> 00:27:55,824
"Descartes"

481
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:09,771
Boy detective! Counting on you!

482
00:28:10,205 --> 00:28:11,106
Sir!

483
00:28:11,173 --> 00:28:13,175
Ran, don't die!

484
00:28:13,275 --> 00:28:15,243
You'd better not die, Ran!

485
00:28:15,310 --> 00:28:17,446
Ran!

486
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:22,951
Ran.
I wouldn't kill someone for your sake.

487
00:28:23,018 --> 00:28:28,256
But...
I would NEVER let one I loved die.

488
00:28:36,298 --> 00:28:38,800
Ran! Are you okay?!

489
00:28:39,735 --> 00:28:41,503
Shin'ichi...

490
00:28:43,638 --> 00:28:45,240
Where's Dad?

491
00:28:46,875 --> 00:28:49,177
He was shut in the room over there.

492
00:28:51,747 --> 00:28:53,048
Eh?!

493
00:29:01,590 --> 00:29:03,792
A balloon?
What on earth is this...

494
00:29:03,925 --> 00:29:08,196
Whoever you are, stop it already!
Stop this balloon!

495
00:29:10,298 --> 00:29:14,136
"Sonoko is Kidnapped!"

496
00:29:17,672 --> 00:29:21,943
"What Lurks Behind
The Beautiful Sister's Inheritance Quarrel"

497
00:29:22,043 --> 00:29:23,812
"This Drama is Fiction"

